WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.501
- My next guest is an awesome

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:04.560
and talented young woman, very talented.

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:06.600
We watched her grow up
on the Disney channel

00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:09.371
and you saw her earlier
this year, along with me,

00:00:09.371 --> 00:00:12.510
in the Netflix film "Feel
the Beat," which I loved.

00:00:12.510 --> 00:00:14.580
She's about to come out with new music,

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:16.920
as well as a new movie called "Songbird."

00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:19.349
Please welcome Sofia Carson, y'all.

00:00:19.349 --> 00:00:24.349
(audience cheering)
(relaxed upbeat music)

00:00:35.370 --> 00:00:36.670
- Hi, guys.
- Oh my gosh.

00:00:36.670 --> 00:00:38.610
So sorry it's awkward.

00:00:38.610 --> 00:00:41.050
- No, I wanna say I'm so happy to be here.

00:00:41.050 --> 00:00:43.150
- I know, I'm glad we've
met already to where

00:00:43.150 --> 00:00:44.570
I've already hugged you
and said hi and everything.

00:00:44.570 --> 00:00:46.240
This would've broken my heart.

00:00:46.240 --> 00:00:48.390
But I met you a long time ago.

00:00:48.390 --> 00:00:49.230
- [Sofia] A long time ago.

00:00:49.230 --> 00:00:51.069
- Yes, and was it with
Cameron at the time?

00:00:51.069 --> 00:00:52.180
- [Sofia] Cam.
- Yes, that's what I thought.

00:00:52.180 --> 00:00:53.460
It was with Cameron.
- Yeah, backstage.

00:00:53.460 --> 00:00:55.410
- Yes, and I literally,

00:00:55.410 --> 00:00:57.160
I knew that y'all were so talented then,

00:00:57.160 --> 00:01:00.400
but I had no idea what
a triple, quadruple,

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:01.800
all the threats you are.
- Oh my gosh.

00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:03.330
Thank you.
- [Kelly] You're so gifted.

00:01:03.330 --> 00:01:04.163
- Thank you, Kelly.

00:01:04.163 --> 00:01:05.890
I mean, coming from you,
and I remember that night

00:01:05.890 --> 00:01:08.470
so vividly at Disney World backstage

00:01:08.470 --> 00:01:10.430
of one of the ABC Christmas specials.

00:01:10.430 --> 00:01:12.510
And you were like imparting
your wisdom on us,

00:01:12.510 --> 00:01:13.747
but like in such a cool way and me

00:01:13.747 --> 00:01:15.170
and Cam were like freaking out.

00:01:15.170 --> 00:01:17.870
- I always tell young people,
I'm like, "Please enjoy it

00:01:17.870 --> 00:01:19.540
and then remember it."

00:01:19.540 --> 00:01:20.590
- That's exactly what you said.

00:01:20.590 --> 00:01:22.082
- Yeah, I'm like, we always just rush

00:01:22.082 --> 00:01:24.010
right through it sometimes
and you're not present.

00:01:24.010 --> 00:01:25.024
We don't--
- [Sofia] Enjoy the ride.

00:01:25.024 --> 00:01:27.430
- We're always worried about
the next job or the next thing

00:01:27.430 --> 00:01:29.023
instead of enjoying like
right where we're at.

00:01:29.023 --> 00:01:31.390
But anyway, you were so
great in "Feel the Beat."

00:01:31.390 --> 00:01:32.890
If y'all didn't see "Feel
the Beat" on Netflix,

00:01:32.890 --> 00:01:33.723
you should check it out.

00:01:33.723 --> 00:01:34.800
I loved it, it was so cute.

00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:36.467
I honestly watched it
'Cause my kids were like,

00:01:36.467 --> 00:01:38.340
"I wanna watch this," my
little girl and I was like,

00:01:38.340 --> 00:01:40.670
I ended up loving it
like just as much as her.

00:01:40.670 --> 00:01:41.503
I was like,

00:01:41.503 --> 00:01:42.336
"This is so great."
- Thank you.

00:01:42.336 --> 00:01:43.169
That means so much to me.

00:01:43.169 --> 00:01:44.530
- I had to tweet about it.

00:01:44.530 --> 00:01:46.850
Anyway, I loved it and
I don't generally tweet

00:01:46.850 --> 00:01:48.270
about everything like that, but--

00:01:48.270 --> 00:01:50.330
- You tweeted and I
almost had a heart attack.

00:01:50.330 --> 00:01:53.557
It was one of those moments
in life where it's like,

00:01:53.557 --> 00:01:57.437
"Oh my gosh, Kelly Clarkson is
watching my movie on Netflix

00:01:57.437 --> 00:01:58.640
"and she tweeted about it."

00:01:58.640 --> 00:01:59.780
I was like, "What is happening?"

00:01:59.780 --> 00:02:01.019
And I screenshot it, sent it to my mom

00:02:01.019 --> 00:02:03.070
and my whole family and
everybody was freaking out.

00:02:03.070 --> 00:02:05.238
And you were just so
generous with what you said,

00:02:05.238 --> 00:02:06.270
so thank you.
- Well, literally,

00:02:06.270 --> 00:02:07.137
I was watching the whole thing going,

00:02:07.137 --> 00:02:09.597
"Oh my gosh, the rehearsals
this must've taken,

00:02:09.597 --> 00:02:12.197
"the discipline," like it's crazy.

00:02:12.197 --> 00:02:14.466
But we were also both at the VMAs, right?

00:02:14.466 --> 00:02:16.590
- We had the trailers next to each other.

00:02:16.590 --> 00:02:17.423
- [Kelly] I did not know that.

00:02:17.423 --> 00:02:19.180
- Literally, I saw your
trailer right there

00:02:19.180 --> 00:02:21.146
and I was like, "Oh, so
close, but so far away."

00:02:21.146 --> 00:02:22.437
- 'Cause, well, it was
weird because I walked in

00:02:22.437 --> 00:02:24.220
and not a soul was in there.

00:02:24.220 --> 00:02:25.975
- No, but they were being
super safe, which was amazing,

00:02:25.975 --> 00:02:27.360
so I didn't see anyone.

00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:29.580
I saw Machine Gun Kelly
from like across the room

00:02:29.580 --> 00:02:32.790
and he's like very tall,
so he was hard to miss,

00:02:32.790 --> 00:02:33.623
but yeah, I didn't see you.

00:02:33.623 --> 00:02:34.470
- I am not tall.

00:02:34.470 --> 00:02:35.447
You can definitely miss me.

00:02:35.447 --> 00:02:36.510
(laughs)
(laughing)

00:02:36.510 --> 00:02:38.510
So you've been singing a long time,

00:02:38.510 --> 00:02:41.340
but what was the first song you learned?

00:02:41.340 --> 00:02:43.540
- The first song I learned

00:02:43.540 --> 00:02:45.970
was actually "Don't Cry for Me Argentina."

00:02:45.970 --> 00:02:47.197
- That is super random.

00:02:47.197 --> 00:02:49.360
(laughs)
- Super random

00:02:49.360 --> 00:02:51.000
and super dramatic.

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:53.430
Like for three, you're right.

00:02:53.430 --> 00:02:55.070
It's very random.

00:02:55.070 --> 00:02:56.710
Yeah, I don't know why.

00:02:56.710 --> 00:02:57.543
Oh, there it is.

00:02:57.543 --> 00:02:58.376
- [Kelly] That's amazing.

00:02:58.376 --> 00:02:59.990
- [Sofia] That's my sister
eating her popsicle,

00:02:59.990 --> 00:03:04.380
super disinterested and me
just having my own little drama

00:03:04.380 --> 00:03:05.690
performance.
- Look at you.

00:03:05.690 --> 00:03:06.523
Look it, shake it.

00:03:06.523 --> 00:03:08.430
(laughs)

00:03:08.430 --> 00:03:11.660
- That was like my outfit, the
bandana and my mom's heels.

00:03:11.660 --> 00:03:15.880
I felt like in that,
that was right for me.

00:03:15.880 --> 00:03:18.987
- I have kids around that
age, so it's cute to see,

00:03:18.987 --> 00:03:20.420
"Oh, one day they're gonna look like you."

00:03:20.420 --> 00:03:21.980
That's crazy, they're gonna be grown up.

00:03:21.980 --> 00:03:23.340
I just got sad.

00:03:23.340 --> 00:03:25.540
So tell me, I want them
to stay little forever.

00:03:25.540 --> 00:03:26.930
So tell me about your new single.

00:03:26.930 --> 00:03:27.980
It's "I Guess I'm a Liar?"

00:03:27.980 --> 00:03:29.160
- Yes, "Guess I'm a Liar."

00:03:29.160 --> 00:03:30.810
It's actually so cool
to be talking about it.

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:34.410
This song, well you're an
incredible musician yourself

00:03:34.410 --> 00:03:36.060
and for me, it's always
been about the stories

00:03:36.060 --> 00:03:40.560
that we get to tell and this
story is a story of survival.

00:03:40.560 --> 00:03:43.159
It's kind of what happens after
your heart's been shattered

00:03:43.159 --> 00:03:46.710
into a million pieces and
you're undeniably sure

00:03:46.710 --> 00:03:49.410
that you can't live without him
and then you wake up one day

00:03:49.410 --> 00:03:51.920
and you realize that you're
alive and you're choosing

00:03:51.920 --> 00:03:53.670
to love yourself better than he ever did.

00:03:53.670 --> 00:03:55.359
So guess I was a liar when I said

00:03:55.359 --> 00:03:57.490
that I couldn't live without you.

00:03:57.490 --> 00:03:58.323
- I love that.

00:03:58.323 --> 00:03:59.433
I love the twist on it.

00:03:59.433 --> 00:04:01.010
That was my favorite part of it.

00:04:01.010 --> 00:04:02.327
So you've also got a new movie,

00:04:02.327 --> 00:04:03.510
"Songbird."
- I do.

00:04:03.510 --> 00:04:04.343
- You are constantly working, girl.

00:04:04.343 --> 00:04:05.840
- Thank you.
- Okay, so how did you

00:04:05.840 --> 00:04:07.220
do all of this in a pandemic?

00:04:07.220 --> 00:04:08.770
- I'm so grateful.

00:04:08.770 --> 00:04:12.790
I was able to shoot the first movie ever

00:04:12.790 --> 00:04:15.270
to be shot during a global
pandemic, which is incredible.

00:04:15.270 --> 00:04:18.070
And I remember recently
I came home from work

00:04:18.070 --> 00:04:19.370
and there was a package at the door,

00:04:19.370 --> 00:04:21.000
which we know is really exciting right now

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:22.630
when we get packages.
- It's like Christmas.

00:04:22.630 --> 00:04:25.428
- And it was from our
producers, from Michael Bay

00:04:25.428 --> 00:04:27.130
and my director, Adam Mason,

00:04:27.130 --> 00:04:31.520
and it was a T-shirt with
the first slate of the movie

00:04:31.520 --> 00:04:33.890
and they said that this
slate will go down in history

00:04:33.890 --> 00:04:36.160
as the first film to ever
be shot during a pandemic,

00:04:36.160 --> 00:04:37.210
so it's incredible.

00:04:37.210 --> 00:04:38.240
I feel so honored.

00:04:38.240 --> 00:04:41.410
- Wow, and speaking of all of this,

00:04:41.410 --> 00:04:43.410
also on a really cool human note,

00:04:43.410 --> 00:04:45.730
you're now a new, you're an
ambassador for UNICEF, right?

00:04:45.730 --> 00:04:47.430
- For UNICEF, yes.
- Yeah, that's great.

00:04:47.430 --> 00:04:48.510
So how did that come about

00:04:48.510 --> 00:04:50.270
and what exactly does that entail?

00:04:50.270 --> 00:04:52.590
Does it kind of happen
after you're allowed

00:04:52.590 --> 00:04:53.810
to start traveling again?

00:04:53.810 --> 00:04:57.070
- Yes, well, I've been supporting
UNICEF for a few years now

00:04:57.070 --> 00:04:59.260
and this also goes back to my mom.

00:04:59.260 --> 00:05:01.400
When I was young, she always
kind of instilled in us

00:05:01.400 --> 00:05:02.940
that the most important
thing that we can to

00:05:02.940 --> 00:05:04.240
is to give back.

00:05:04.240 --> 00:05:06.180
And she would always
refer to Audrey Hepburn,

00:05:06.180 --> 00:05:09.300
who was the first UNICEF
ambassador and who was my icon.

00:05:09.300 --> 00:05:11.920
And now to be, to join
those ranks and to be able

00:05:11.920 --> 00:05:13.360
to be a UNICEF ambassador

00:05:13.360 --> 00:05:16.200
is the most important
thing that I'll ever do

00:05:16.200 --> 00:05:19.010
and I'm so honored and
it basically means yes,

00:05:19.010 --> 00:05:20.330
I do get to go on field trips

00:05:20.330 --> 00:05:22.470
and I once traveled to Brazil with them

00:05:22.470 --> 00:05:24.688
and I see firsthand like the
schools that they're building.

00:05:24.688 --> 00:05:27.600
The girls that they actually
save through education,

00:05:27.600 --> 00:05:30.170
which is kind of like where my heart lies

00:05:30.170 --> 00:05:31.650
and I'm just so thrilled to see

00:05:31.650 --> 00:05:32.840
where this journey will take us.

00:05:32.840 --> 00:05:33.673
- Me as well.

00:05:33.673 --> 00:05:35.150
I think it's really key
too 'cause right now,

00:05:35.150 --> 00:05:37.640
'cause I have kids and
my mom was a teacher,

00:05:37.640 --> 00:05:39.570
and education is so important

00:05:39.570 --> 00:05:40.510
and we take it for granted

00:05:40.510 --> 00:05:41.423
in this country.
- Because we don't

00:05:41.423 --> 00:05:42.310
have to think about it.
- How it's offered

00:05:42.310 --> 00:05:44.092
because we don't think about
it and now that our kids are,

00:05:44.092 --> 00:05:46.677
my kids are dying to go to school.

00:05:46.677 --> 00:05:47.510
- [Sofia] How beautiful is that?

00:05:47.510 --> 00:05:49.100
My little boy's actually able to go,

00:05:49.100 --> 00:05:51.500
but my little girl's dying
to physically be in school.

00:05:51.500 --> 00:05:52.600
- Because they know what
it's like to not have it.

00:05:52.600 --> 00:05:54.670
- 'Cause now they know what
it's like to not have that

00:05:54.670 --> 00:05:56.350
and it's been kind of taken away,

00:05:56.350 --> 00:05:59.747
but well, Sofia's new single, y'all.

00:05:59.747 --> 00:06:01.660
"I Guess I'm a Liar" is out right now.

00:06:01.660 --> 00:06:03.700
Y'all gotta check it
and be sure to check out

00:06:03.700 --> 00:06:05.950
her new movie "Songbird" in theaters soon

00:06:05.950 --> 00:06:08.350
'cause she has all the
projects going on, y'all.

